<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly softer to steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly softer to steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly softer on Tuesday as the Central Bank kept its overnight rates at present levels, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is very liquid on both dollars and the pesos so swap rates are lower,&quot; said a senior bank trader.</p>
<p>But banks remained cautious on prospects in the medium and long term, traders said.</p>
<p>The six-month and one-year bills were steady on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>		    June 17		 June 16</p>
<p> 1 W		12			12  1/4</p>
<p> 2 W		11  3/4		 12</p>
<p> 1 M		11  5/16		11  3/8</p>
<p> 2 M		11  5/16		11  3/8</p>
<p> 3 M		11  3/8		 11  7/16</p>
<p> 6 M		11  7/16		11  7/16</p>
<p> 12M		11  3/8		 11  3/8</p>
<p> VAL		18-Jun		  17-Jun</p>
<p>-- Dolly Aglay (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
